# Git hooks must be LF in the working tree on every platform. A hook checked out with CRLF
# fails as "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M", which reads as a broken script rather than as a
# line-ending problem and costs an hour to recognise. core.autocrlf is not set anywhere in
# this clone, so this file is the only thing pinning it.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
